You should clear out Gehennom and make everything ready for 
the ascension run _before_ going to Rodney.  It's not nice 
to have him on your tail permanently while you're still looking 
for the Vibrating Square.  Be sure to visit Vlad first.  

> Paul the Enchanter
> St: 18 Dx: 17 Co: 16 In: 19 Wi: 18 CH: 8 Chaotic
> HP: 102 Pw: 199 AC: -23 XP: 14

If you have spare wishes or some polypile ressources, 
try to get gauntlets of dexterity and a helm of brilliance 
to improve spellcasting.  Additionally, use magic markers 
(can be polypiled from other magic tools, like unicorn 
horns) to improve your AC.  Even more important, at least 
double (better triple) your HP by alchemy, nurses and 
golden glows.  

> Inventory: (I'll take out items that are pretty generic...)
> blessed Eye of the Aethiopica (worn)
> +0 silver saber (alternate weapon)
> +1 Magicbane (weilded)

If you want to rely on Magicbane, you'll need to cast 
spells.  The Amulet of Yendor will make casting more 
expensive, so maybe you should look for an alternate 
Hack'n'slash weapon, and change from a robe to a 
cloak of MR.  Frost Brand is great, and Stormbringer 
is also a nice weapon (but be careful with it).  
The latter is given to you when you're crowned, so 
no need for a wish.  

> ring of fire resistance (worn)
> ring of regeneration
> ring of conflict
> ring of teleport control (worn)

A = of free action can be nice here.  And I think you should 
try to get crowned if you don't have fire resistance yet.  
Teleport control can be gained by eating tengi, which 
one can reverse-genocide (frees a ring slot).  

> wand of teleportation 

Try to get loads of these, for later use in Gehennom 
(speeds up your escape significantly to repeatedly zap 
yourself while having tele control).  

> wand of polymorph

If you want to polypile, gather all junk that can potentially 
be polyied into something valuable, then carefully build 
four heaps or so, and empty the wand, always checking for 
new nice stuff.  Poly first, wish later.  Remember that most 
of the times, magic foo is polyied from magic foo, so poly 
elven cloaks and boots, boots of fumbling etc., and unicorn 
horns, magic whistles etc.. Check the poly spoilers for 
details how to arrange things to avoid golems.  

> So my questions are, should I wish for anything? My last wish was for
> a blessed magic marker, and it gave me about 3 enchant armour scrolls
> then dried up ...

Also polypile for scrolls of charging.  

> Also is there anything I should do before going on?

You should have with you:  

- some potions of full healing (real lifesavers), 
  one (q)uaff--ready at all times, 

- enough food and then some (K-rations preferably), 

- half a dozen wands of digging, 

- four scrolls of gold detection, 

- some means to confuse yourself, 

- a backup weapon for the not--all--too unlikely event 
  that somebody (a)pplies a whip to snatch your weapon, 

- maybe a sack to hide your boH in (you don't want to have 
  it unblessed), 

- some means to blind yourself, 

Unless you're all over the challenge of genoless, genocide some 
nasties; Ls, hs, ;s can lead to annoying situations.  


